      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by:\n\n1. **Not holding the key in the Hub\u0027s process**: The Hub\u0027s own environment is never mutated with the API key.\n\n2. **Using a local secrets loader**: At startup, a local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file.\n\n3. **Injecting only into child processes**: The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest agent and Query agent), immediately before those processes start.\n\n4. **Isolating the credential to short-lived processes**: The key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.\n\nThis design ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, the API key cannot be leaked simply by inspecting the Hub\u0027s own environment variables \u2014 the credential is kept entirely outside the Hub\u0027s memory space.",
      "input_tokens": 2516,
      "output_tokens": 212
    }
